; selftest-refuse.eval - handed to the runner by `Eval.ps1 -SelfTest`; must PASS.
;
; The half of `expect-refuse` that keeps a probe from failing its own run: each
; probe below is refused by the command's own rule, so none of them counts, and
; each stands beside a CONTROL the same command accepts - a probe that passed
; because the command refused everything would fail on its control.
; (0,0 of the demo's world map is water and 6,6 its authored start, so the
; control moves nothing; `fyre` is not a skill - C446.)
logecho on
reset
worldprops start 6 6
expect-refuse worldprops start 0 0
expect-refuse setskill 0 fyre 2
setskill 0 fire 2
; The editor's erase and move report what HAPPENED (C442): a square with an
; override pinned erases once, then has nothing left to erase; a barrel moves
; once, then neither a drop where it lies nor a drop on rock moves it (EndMove's
; two refusals); a square with nothing on it has nothing to move; and a verb
; nobody wrote is refused.
editor fill floors floor_slabs rect 3 3 3 3
editor erase 3 3
expect-refuse editor erase 3 3
editor place decorations barrel 3 5
editor move 3 5 4 5
expect-refuse editor move 4 5 4 5
expect-refuse editor move 4 5 0 5
expect-refuse editor move 3 3 4 4
expect-refuse editor nosuchverb
editor off
state
